/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  VMFL006 -- Multicomponent Species Transport in Pipe Flow
  (Ansys Fluid Dynamics Verification Manual, Release 2026 R1, pp. 27-28).

  Axisymmetric WEDGE, one cell thick, `wedge` front/back patches -- the v2606
  idiom already proven in this team on VMFL003/VMFL005/VMFL007.  Reused as SETUP
  KNOWLEDGE ONLY: no gate, band or reference of those cases is reused and no
  frozen file of theirs is touched.

  Pipe axis is +x, 0 <= x <= L = 0.1 m; radius R = 0.0025 m (manual p.27).
  Wall vertices sit at EXACT radius R:
        y_w = R cos(2.5 deg) = 0.0024976205539546445
        z_w = R sin(2.5 deg) = 1.0904846841334003e-04
  so |(y_w, z_w)| = R to machine precision (NOT y = R, z = R tan a, which would
  put the wall at R/cos a).

  AXIAL: UNIFORM, __NX__ cells, and __NX__ is ALWAYS A MULTIPLE OF 10, so a mesh
  FACE lies exactly at each of the ten gate stations x = 0.01 ... 0.10 m on every
  level of the grid family.  The mixing-cup average is then taken on REAL MESH
  FACES carrying the solver's OWN conserved flux -- nothing is interpolated onto
  a constructed plane.

  RADIAL: GRADED FINE AT THE WALL, total ratio __RGRAD__ (last cell / first cell
  = 0.25, i.e. 4x refinement towards the wall).  The concentration boundary layer
  grows from the wall and is thinnest at the first gate station (delta/R ~
  sqrt(2 tau) = 0.15 at x = 0.01 m), which is exactly where the gate is tightest.
  The total ratio is HELD FIXED across the whole r = 2 family, so doubling __NR__
  halves the wall cell -- a clean ratio-2 family in the near-wall spacing too.

  N-AV9 -- THE AZIMUTHAL DEFICIT IS NOT REMOVED BY THIS MESH OR BY ANY REFINEMENT
  OF IT.  A flat-sided 5 deg wedge has cross-sectional area 0.9987312439537492 of
  the true circular sector (deficit 0.1268756046250763 %) and wall area
  0.9996827203920081 of the true arc (deficit 0.03172796079918827 %); their ratio
  is exactly sec(2.5 deg) = 1.0009526851633199.  The wedge volumetric flow rate is
  therefore 0.5*sin(5 deg)*R^2*Uavg = 2.7236169608643178e-07 m3/s, NOT the true
  sector value pi*R^2*(5/360)*Uavg = 2.7270769562411397e-07 m3/s.  The frozen
  conservation control in grade_vmfl006.py uses the FLAT-WEDGE value.  The signed
  effect on the GRADED quantity is carried in PREREGISTRATION.md sec.11.

  __NX__, __NR__, __RGRAD__ substituted by run_vmfl006.sh; this template is never
  edited by a run.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       dictionary;
    object      blockMeshDict;
}

mergeType points;   // wedge geometry -- merge the coincident axis points

scale   1;

vertices
(
    (0.0  0                       0                      )   // 0  inlet  axis
    (0.1  0                       0                      )   // 1  outlet axis
    (0.0  0.0024976205539546445  -1.0904846841334003e-04 )   // 2  inlet  wall back
    (0.1  0.0024976205539546445  -1.0904846841334003e-04 )   // 3  outlet wall back
    (0.0  0.0024976205539546445   1.0904846841334003e-04 )   // 4  inlet  wall front
    (0.1  0.0024976205539546445   1.0904846841334003e-04 )   // 5  outlet wall front
);

blocks
(
    hex (0 1 3 2  0 1 5 4) (__NX__ __NR__ 1) simpleGrading (1 __RGRAD__ 1)
);

edges
(
);

boundary
(
    inlet  { type patch; faces ( (0 2 4 0) ); }
    outlet { type patch; faces ( (1 3 5 1) ); }
    walls  { type wall;  faces ( (2 3 5 4) ); }
    wedge1 { type wedge; faces ( (0 2 3 1) ); }
    wedge2 { type wedge; faces ( (0 1 5 4) ); }
);

mergePatchPairs
(
);
